{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Intro - Chorus instrumental
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
We [E]started out from Bern one [C#m]sunny August morn
[A]There was just the four of us against the [E]Matterhorn
There was [C#m]Albert the Australian and [E]John the Irishman
[A]Me and Bill from Britain, mad dogs in the [E]sun
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C#m]Matterhorn, Matterhorn
[C#m]Men have tried and [E]men have died to [A]climb the [E]Matterhorn
That [A]mighty [E]Matterhorn
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Two miles up we lost John and our rations fell below
Now Al and Bill are lying beneath an avalanche of snow
Now here I am alone and I know I cannot stop
Two more yards in front of me before I reach the top
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Now here I am a dying upon the Matterhorn
Not a thing for me to lie in or a thing to keep me warm
The queen would surely knight me if I could get back down
But it's closer here to heaven than it is back to the ground
{end_of_chorus}
